id: decisions/039-scoring-record-points-at-receipt
title: "A move-scoring record points at its receipt"
kind: decision-frame
record_shape: header
status: draft
authored_by: agent-on-behalf
authored_via: "Claude Code session on Dave's behalf, 2026-09-12; drafted from the JUDGMENTS.md reversal axis 'how-success-is-judged'; recommendation is an attributed inference and ratifies nothing"
version: "1.0.0"
updated: 2026-09-12
template_ref: templates/decision.yawn
principal_ref: principal:dave

axis: how-success-is-judged
axis_gloss: "whether the actor that made the move declares it succeeded, or a separate step or party evaluates the outcome"
poles:
  a: independently-evaluated-success
  b: self-certified-success
split: lone-exception
draft_status: full
leverage: 6.7
leverage_formula: "judgments_resolved(14) x split_weight(0.4) x authored_conflict_bonus(1.2)"

question: >
  Is a move's success always judged by a separate observation and receipt — and
  if so, where does a record that ranks and suggests moves write, or point to,
  what actually happened?

why_it_matters: >
  'A move cannot mark itself successful' is authored in four core files and
  enforced by role splits (verifier never co-occurs with actor), yet
  templates/next-move-record.yawn scores, suggests and sets replay_after with no
  slot for the observed outcome, so the loop it starts can never close inside
  the record. Once answered, a bot that ranks its next move knows it must leave
  a pointer to the receipt a verifier will write, and a verifier knows where to
  attach it.

state_snapshot:
  description: >
    13 judgments sit at independently-evaluated-success (9 authored) and 1 at
    self-certified-success (0 authored). The repository asserts both directions on
    this axis.
  attributed_to: JUDGMENTS.md
  epistemic_status: observed
  source_refs:
    - JUDGMENTS.md
    - TAXONOMY.md

lacuna:
  kind: unselected_choice
  description: >
    Whether Dave wants the scoring record to be incomplete (a lacuna) while
    result_ref is empty, or merely open.

options:
  - name: A
    description: >
      rule: Every record that proposes, ranks or performs a move carries an outcome
      block (observed_delta, observed_by, evidence) that only an actor other than
      the proposer may fill. templates/next-move-record.yawn gains that block.
    cost: "One block in one template; guidance on who may fill it."
    risk: "The scoring record becomes the place the outcome is written, so the actor who wrote the score is now editing the same file as the judge."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "New assertion in tests/record-shape.test.mjs: every template whose kind names a move (next-move-record, decision, structural-change-receipt, turn) carries an outcome or transition_result block with an observed_by field."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0081"
      - "J0145"
      - "J0209"
      - "J0410"
      - "J0529"
      - "J0546"
  - name: B
    description: >
      rule: The actor that made the move may record its own result. A move record
      ends when the actor says it ended.
    cost: "Strikes 'A move cannot mark itself successful.' from core/proof-and-boundary.yawn transition_boundary and the matching invariants in core/state-transition.yawn, core/turn.yawn, core/movement-loop.yawn and question-packets/turn-close.yawn."
    risk: "Every receipt in records/ becomes self-certification; the interception result test ('the result proves the bounded candidate') no longer means anything."
    reversibility: false
    proof_needed: "None can enforce self-certification; the record would be the five deletions above."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0845"
  - name: C
    description: >
      rule: Success is judged by a separate observation and receipt, always. A
      record that ranks or suggests moves never writes the outcome; it carries
      result_ref: (empty until a verifier writes a proof-receipt) and is incomplete
      until that pointer resolves. templates/next-move-record.yawn gains result_ref:
      and a sentence saying who fills it.
    cost: "One field and one sentence in one template; a receipt per suggested move that gets acted on."
    risk: "result_ref stays empty forever and nothing notices."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "Extend tests/record-shape.test.mjs: a template of kind next-move-record carries result_ref:; extend scripts/validate-proof-refs.mjs so a non-empty result_ref must resolve to a record whose observed_by or verifier differs from the scoring record's actor."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0081"
      - "J0410"
      - "J0529"
      - "J0546"
      - "J0845"

recommendation:
  option_ref: C
  confidence: 0.75
  epistemic_status: inferred
  authority: none
  reasoning: >
    Nine authored judgments say the actor is never the judge; the lone exception
    is not a claim of self-certification but a template with nowhere to close the
    loop. A would give the scoring record an outcome slot, which puts actor and
    judge in one file; C keeps the separation the role split (J0410) and the
    proof_refs pattern (J0546, outcome-attached) already use, and costs one
    pointer field. Confidence is high because both authored rule and existing
    practice point the same way; the only question is the field name.

target_condition:
  mode: decide
  proposed_by: agent-on-behalf
  affected_principals:
    - principal:dave
  ratification_status: proposed
  sufficient_when:
    - "templates/next-move-record.yawn carries result_ref: with a sentence saying a verifier other than the proposer fills it."
    - "A test in tests/ rejects a move-ranking template without result_ref and passes."
    - "Any non-empty result_ref in records/ resolves to a receipt whose verifier is not the scoring record's actor, and validate-proof-refs checks it."

choice:
  selected_by: ""
  option_ref: ""
  authority_ref: ""

proof:
  covers:
    - target_condition
    - options
  falsifier: >
    A next-move record in records/ carries a filled outcome written by the same
    agent that scored the move, and nothing fails.
  status: proposed

resolves:
  - "J0081"
  - "J0145"
  - "J0209"
  - "J0410"
  - "J0529"
  - "J0546"
  - "J0845"

boundary:
  - "confidence cannot ratify an objective; this record proposes and Dave decides"
  - "the REVEALED judgments cited here describe what artifacts do, not what Dave chose"

source:
  template: templates/decision.yawn
  axis: TAXONOMY.md
  inventory: JUDGMENTS.md
